<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Onjo of Baekje</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Onjo is the legendary founder of Baekje, said by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samguk-sagi">Samguk sagi</a> to have been a son of Jumong, founder of Goguryeo. According to tradition, he left the north with followers and founded the kingdom in 18 BCE at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wiryeseong">Wiryeseong</a>, on the Han river near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seoul">Seoul</a>, while his brother Biryu settled at Michuhol. Historians treat the account as legend reflecting Baekje's origins among migrants from the north.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/onjo-of-baekje.jpg" alt="Onjo of Baekje" width="263" height="434" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Jeong Inho Transcription: History Net, National Institute of Korean History · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%EC%B4%88%EB%93%B1%EB%8C%80%ED%95%9C%EC%97%AD%EC%82%AC_%EC%A0%9C2%ED%8E%B8_12.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
